  "brief": "READ-ONLY #972 ENGINEERING HANDOFF — 2026-10-06\n\nCurrent preflight main ebfc498397c64706177cc8d885d916d446fe19a8. #972, #242 and #243 have no canonical reservation comment; #1106 has a released reservation (active:false, live_work:false). Recheck claims and actual latest main before implementation. No claims, edits to tracked files, PRs, provider/browser/database operations or deployment occurred.\n\nUse R=research/geography/shared-seam-prt-esp-20261006/, merged PR1123 at1ba7ef86a046db62c2c19d731faf8118e6cee124. Run10 report549069bytes SHA4f52d5ef455ae24e4ec7d0067567e6498e7407a0244a08622c3e2793ed0ad5a0. Original execution992cd13dfbc74af7669029c4104af390993e5471. Earlier trials remain archival; run09/run10 are final byte-identical pair. Report input_files is the exact whole-file input inventory copied into this handoff.\n\nAvailable originals: four DGT full municipality responses (Castelo Branco0502, Idanha-a-Nova0505, Vila Velha de Rodao0511, Nisa1212) and eight full IGN administrativeunit responses (1172975,1173013,1173029,1173031,1173060,1173085,1173135,1173184). Their twelve actual Git file bytes were checked against run10 descriptors on preflight main; total8517055bytes. Before Atlas full parts19/28 and hierarchy/grid manifests also still match the report. Separate eight2022 IGN boundary-line items, country control5702440 and interior negative control5673087 are retained originals; lines cannot substitute for polygon coverage. Original Spanish roster has55members belonging to three Atlas districts; retain every source-member crosswalk. Zarza la Mayor is resolved by nationalcode34111010218, not proximity or guessed name.\n\nInputs: full component gap:ad2052defbeba8e89287bcc4344e641225c6579f9afd584497b381fe8fd8eedc in components-004.json.gz; containing-file SHA c8726499e2d34c89b45fcf5d4c725b9583d2cb14319736580c032d460c04cb54. Current release pointer after1150 must be pinned separately; do not relabel archived v6 evaluation as a fresh v7 measurement.\n\nSmallest next delivery: a new immutable engineering full-component diagnostic partition producer, no core edit. Read Git blobs and verify complete mandatory source custody. Preserve seven subjects and actual neighbors. With unchanged official unions P and S and full gap G, export Portugal-only G intersect(P minus S), Spain-only G intersect(S minus P), both G intersect P intersect S, neither G minus(P union S), plus every per-member/contact/lower-dimensional remainder, invalidity and operation failure. Compare complete reconstructed covered/residual shapes to archived run10 and whole current subjects. No geometry is assigned an Atlas owner by this analysis. Commit producer before two complete new owned runs and compare every output.\n\nReuse pure projected/geometry_record/geometry_parts/gap_coverage_record logic from R/scripts/reproduce-comparison.py under pinned full closure. Do not run its main CLI: it writes research-owned paths and pins old release. Area policy is CRS84 longitude/latitude projected to EPSG25829, ETRS89/UTM29N; numerical areas are planar, not WGS84 ellipsoidal. Runtime recorded Python3.12.14/Shapely2.1.2/GEOS3.13.1/PyProj3.7.2/PROJ9.5.1. No current performance claim.\n\nControls: all four partition classes, overlaps, holes, tiny polygons, point-only contacts, invalid geometry, altered/omitted members, source/CRS pin failures, overwrite rejection, and complete shape reconstruction. Check pairwise interior disjointness and retain actual reconstruction differences, not area-only equality. Do not snap/buffer/make-valid/simplify/nearest-fill/discard small residues or waive limits. Use typed positive-control/negative-control/reproducibility receipts and exact source/release/grid pins. GEOS structural differences and lower-dimensional remnants must remain visible rather than being cleared with epsilon.\n\nCustody: existing216MiB research packet remains immutable in primary Git. New engineering consumer needs only actual12small polygon originals plus required source/metadata/item/crosswalk receipts. A mandatory separately bounded source-custody stage can verify existing full original partitions and provenance without duplicating them into output; never rename extracts as original packets. Full Spanish raw149105849B SHA ccce612ee6275d91e2d2fcccf7912087dcc72377abec6c8e20c65089ecb48564 is distinct from baseline simplified18613175B SHA e5bfa1c3889ea763ca2bb82c7f1e8ff9eff715dcb99ce405293a03de7ac85862. Portugal raw415110B SHA a02fd52278e5e300a19949450e793812fe76d78664c0a896bb3c5ebda7f79f9e is distinct from simplified387331B SHA f7a9143190715b85812b03617adc4879898b8c6a6789b9c9732c9705ea6c21ac. IGN bbox discovery136542585B SHA112b21ea6e3afd1503558bde7a4c771378ed458dd1f41dd8a6021a17205704f0 is retained lossless discovery response, not national export or clipped original.\n\nLimits: no DGT national GPKG or CNIG national SHP/GML downloaded; no verified bilateral registered coordinate annex, no Spanish polygon validity date, no dated local physical-water source. IGN item agreed status is not bilateral legal authority; country control has nil legalstatus. CAOP2025 collection declares conflicting2000-2007 temporal extent. Surface/seasonality/datum/registration remain unknown. IGN/DGT reuse attribution CC-BY4; geoBoundaries Spain CC-BY4 and Portugal CC0 notices retained. Original report residual27087.655736m2 is available full MultiPolygon; it is not approved water or proof of repair.\n",
